*  ΔS(PbS) = 91.2 J/K mol
*  ΔS(O2) = 205.1 J/K mol
*  ΔS(PbO) = 66.5  S/K mol
*  ΔS(SO2) = 248.2  S/K mol

Now, let calculate the change in entropy:

ΔS = (2 * ΔS(PbO) + 2 * ΔS(S2O2)) - (2 * ΔS(PbS) + 3 * ΔS(O2))
ΔS = (2 * 66.5 + 2 * 248.2) - (2 * 91.2 + 3 * 205.1)
ΔS = (133 + 496.4) - (182.4 + 615.3)
ΔS = 529.4 - 787.7
ΔS = -257.3

