What is the number of chloride ions produced when the complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` (tetraamminedichloroplatinum(IV) chloride) is dissolved in an aqueous solution?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","Let the complex is [Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2.
When this complex is dissolved in an aqueous solution, it will dissociate into ions.
The complex is [Pt(NH3)4Cl2]2+ and Cl2-.
So, the equation is:
[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]2+ + Cl2-  →  [Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2
When [Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2 is dissolved in an aqueous solution, it will dissociate into the following ions:
[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]2+ + 2Cl-
